# base differential (cases) — failures that have been ADJUDICATED, NOT zcc bugs.
# float_h: a DELIBERATE, DOCUMENTED deviation from the standard (MILESTONES M15). zcc chooses
#   `long double = double` on ELF — VALID under C99 §5.2.4.2.2 (which only requires LD ≥
#   double; MSVC makes the same choice); float.h declares LDBL_MANT_DIG=53 for SELF-
#   CONSISTENCY (memory remains binary128 for ABI interop). Linux cc uses binary128
#   (LDBL_MANT_DIG=113) hence the diff — the ONLY objective failure in the box, exactly as
#   anticipated. On macOS (Darwin LD=double) this case PASSES.
float_h
